The data is somebody else's, and carries its own terms
------------------------------------------------------

This project reads open geodata published by the German state surveying
authorities, by the Bundesamt für Kartographie und Geodäsie, and by the
Copernicus programme. Each of those datasets is licensed by whoever published
it — mostly under `dl-de/by-2-0`, `dl-de/zero-2-0` or `CC BY 4.0` — and most of
them **require a named credit wherever the data is shown**.

A height displayed without its credit is a height used outside its licence.

One of them ships inside this repository and its image rather than being
fetched: `ninanatur/data/climate_de.json.gz`, the growing season's light
climate, made by `scripts/dwd_climate.py` from the Deutscher Wetterdienst's
Climate Data Center grids (global and diffuse radiation, sunshine duration).
It is licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/)
and **changed**: 1 km cells averaged to 10 km, and the diffuse fraction computed
from two of the grids. Its credit, in the DWD's own wording for averaged
values: "Datenbasis: Deutscher Wetterdienst, Einzelwerte gemittelt".

The required credit for every source is carried in the code beside the source
itself, and is served to the page that shows the number, so that showing a
value and showing its provenance are one act rather than two. See
`.mdd/docs/106-which-source-said-so.md`.


